  "name": "Figures With Multiple Layers",
  "problem": "If a figure has multiple layers, we can find its volume by first finding the volume of each layer and then adding the results.\n\nEach cube in the figure below represents one cubic unit. Let's find its volume.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/547a09fed5b5b736b556db4d476f869a68a39528f59d6a5abe505f1fa38260d9.png)\n\nThe figure consists of two layers:\n\n- The bottom layer consists of $2$ cubes.\n\n- The top layer consists of $2$ cubes, too.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/6b7e4ce3ffa821b4263213782bf99a4243f3b844c862e49fcf5181a6f4cdacd2.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume is $2+2=4$ cubic units.",
